{
  "requirement": "An execution error returns `Err` rather than a `Fingerprinted` containing a\ncompleted answer.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.validators.validate_node.errors`.\n\n**Obligation.** When `verify` hits an execution error, it must return `Err`. It must not return a `Fingerprinted` that holds a completed answer. The input classes that matter are the different sources of execution error.\n\n**Coverage by source of error:**\n- **Criterion `execute` fails.** In `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[loading_execution_resolution_and_saving_failures_do_not_publish_answers]`, `review.failure = Some(\"execute\")` makes `verify` return `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"execute\"))`.\n- **Input resolution fails.** In the same test, reading a missing `Node(99)` returns `Err(Graph(\"missing\"))`. A `fail_edges` failure returns `Err(Graph(\"edges\"))`.\n- **Node read fails inside the callback.** In `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]`, `read_in_callback` returns `Err(Graph(\"missing\"))`. The test also asserts that no record is stored.\n- **Output decode fails inside `execute`.** In `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer]`, non-JSON content returns `Err(ValidationError::Output)`, and no record is stored.\n  - The same test checks the contrast the requirement draws. A negative answer (`false`) is a completed answer: `verify` returns `Ok` with the fingerprinted dependency.\n- **No agent configured.** In `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]`, `verify` returns `Err(NoAgentConfigured)`, and the state holds no record. Once an agent is added, `verify` succeeds.\n- **Execution after stale or bad evidence.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence]` and `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs#fn[malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors]` check that a fresh `verify` still runs and returns `Ok` when the failure was only in loading. This confirms that `Err` is tied to execution errors.\n\nAll the error assertions use `matches!` on the specific `Err` variant, so a `Fingerprinted` returned in an error case would fail them. The tests also check that no evidence is written or published after the error. They cover several kinds of execution error and the contrasting success cases, so I found no gap.",
  "references": "ca528c7ab9a4fa85f00a0c070782b2ef35dae1770f605645ea19157fe7e8b575",
